body:
Reference direction across library layers: section calls resolve across the merged library, so a local template invokes an external section template with the `section` helper exactly as it invokes a local one (section-helper). The external layer is a self-contained library: every template, theme and media reference inside an external-layer template resolves within the external library alone, so the external library validates on its own as a standalone library before the merge (templates-dir-validation). A reference from an external template to a section, theme or media name that only the local layer carries is a templates error, while a reference from a local template to an external name resolves.

AC:
- a local slide template whose layout calls an external section template renders that external section;
- a local theme or layout that references an external `media/` file resolves;
- an external template that references a section or media file carried only by the local layer is a templates error naming the external template;
- the external library validates as a standalone library with the local `templates/` directory absent.
